{"seq":9,"id":"01M8D4E8WB3HG6EQNF4YG567H2","cdr":"CDR-0001","attempt":"CDR-0001-A1","type":"agent.result","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"implementer","adapter":"claude-opus"},"at":"2026-11-26T23:53:19.499Z","payload":{"role":"implementer","adapter":"claude-opus","result_sha256":"458e67fd88542f7d30266e913daa8278ae9a4c0e49d2b7f762211c345eec36bd","result":{"summary":"I added packages/ui-kit/agent/flavour.md, a one-page flavour contract in three parts. Part 1 is a table of the 12 brand traits. Each trait cites where it comes from in design-language.md (L1–L6), and the one-accent rule cites Decision 2. Part 2 is the bezel card: owner pick of 2026-11-27, marked as chosen but not yet shipped, with frame and stage, concentric radii (r6 + 8 = r14), alpha-hairline edges with no CSS border, and a caption row. Part 3 is the do-not-converge table. Each item names the rule it breaks, and the blur item and the figurative-art item are credited to the owner. I also added one flavour.md row to the file table in packages/ui-kit/agent/README.md. No CSS, JS, tokens or package.json changed, and design-language.md was not touched. There were no frozen tests, and I did not run any checks.","assumptions":["The `agent/` entry in the files list and the `./agent/*` export already cover the new flavour.md, so package.json does not change.","The blur ban covers blur used as transition material only. The standing blur materials in design-language.md (the sticky header, the palette) stay as they are, and flavour.md says so.","The figurative-art ruling is credited only to the owner, with no L3 citation. L3 Art still describes the 0.45 posters with hills and plants, so citing it would be inaccurate."],"risks":["The README sentence that lists what the agent core holds does not name flavour.md. The CDR allowed only the new table row.","If a test checks the agent/*.md files for structure or tables, it might flag the new file. I did not run any tests."],"disputes":[],"follow_ups":[{"title":"Write the 2026-11-27 dissolve-over-blur and bezel decisions into design-language.md","why":"flavour.md credits both to the owner and the date because design-language.md does not record them yet; the grammar file should be the authority."},{"title":"Reconcile L3 Art (0.45 posters with hills and plants) with the no-figurative-art ruling","why":"design-language.md L3 still describes posters with organic plant and landscape imagery, which conflicts with the owner's later no-figurative-art ruling cited in flavour.md."}],"learnings":["design-language.md L3 Art still describes figurative 0.45 posters (hills, plants), so do not cite it for the no-figurative-art ruling.","design-language.md keeps blur as a material (sticky header, palette); the 2026-11-27 ban applies only to blur used as a transition."]}},"cost":{"tokens_in":12,"tokens_out":4603,"tokens_cache_write":62942,"tokens_cache_read":238706,"seconds":53.402172875,"usd":0.6433852},"signer":"ads-team:marcello.barile@gmail.com","prev_hash":"77294e81bc3f3149769c3e5903e341c5859a6a41fe72521d89e92c28cc2f7488","hash":"14b20c701f57628791cfe385db887966d76d419c24291cdda7d5c6dd870cff34","sig":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgt+9LVHCb4CLBAIrBcP4iIkhhc+\nSCDbAr1oNRi9kG2bAAAAAJYWRzLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1l\nZDI1NTE5AAAAQJL4PRI3VC1YIK0Aw8WJBktCGb7NP/HpGn99ImWWc/wc71zUfM66pLStqq\nu6v2J/JjMBr4o6KlqFYi69x6T3Tw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----\n"}
